# Surya Photography Website — User Manual

## 1) What this website is
This website has two parts:
- Public website (for customers): Home, Portfolio, About, Contact
- Admin panel (for studio staff): Manage portfolio uploads, inquiries, bookings (functions), and studio details

Open links (default local):
- Website: http://localhost:3000
- Admin Login: http://localhost:3000/admin/login

## 2) Public Website (Customer Side)

### 2.1 Home page ("/")
What you can do:
- View the main hero slideshow (featured photos/videos)
- Scroll down to see “Featured Categories”
- View “Latest Works” gallery
- Read “Customer Reviews”
- Use the WhatsApp button to message the studio
- Use the Contact Details button to open the Contact page

How to use it step-by-step:
1. Open the website.
2. Scroll slowly to explore each section.
3. To see a full gallery, click “Explore Full Portfolio” or open “Portfolio” from the top menu.

### 2.2 Top menu navigation
The top menu has:
- Home
- Portfolio
- About
- Contact

Mobile menu:
- Tap the menu button on the top right to open/close navigation links.

### 2.3 Portfolio page ("/portfolio")
What you see:
- A grid of categories (example: Wedding, Baby Shower, Outdoor, etc.)
- Each category shows photo count and video count

How to open a category:
1. Go to Portfolio.
2. Click any category card.
3. You will be taken to that category’s page.

### 2.4 Category page ("/portfolio/<category>")
What you can do:
- Browse photos and videos for that category
- Play videos directly on the page (if videos exist)

If a category is missing:
- You may see a “Not Found” page. This means the category does not exist or the API is not reachable.

### 2.5 About page ("/about")
What you see:
- Studio story text
- Founder/owner portrait (if uploaded from Admin)
- Studio “events covered / years / happy families” counters
- Contact details section

### 2.6 Contact page ("/contact")
What you can do:
- Tap “WhatsApp Us” to open WhatsApp chat
- Tap “Call …” to call from your phone
- View studio contact details
- View location map (only if a Google Maps embed link is set in Admin)

## 3) Admin Panel (Studio Staff Side)

### 3.1 How to open Admin Login
There are two ways:
1. Direct link: http://localhost:3000/admin/login
2. Hidden shortcut:
   - Scroll to the bottom footer on any public page.
   - Quickly click 5 times on the “© … Surya Photography …” footer text.
   - Admin Login page opens automatically.

### 3.2 Admin Login ("/admin/login")
Fields:
- Username (email)
- Password

Steps:
1. Enter the admin username.
2. Enter the admin password.
3. Click “Sign In”.
4. After login, you are redirected to the Admin Dashboard.

If login fails:
- You will see “Invalid username or password”.
- Confirm you are typing the correct password.
- If credentials were changed, use the updated username/password.

### 3.3 Admin Navigation (left sidebar on desktop / bottom nav on mobile)
Menu items:
- Dashboard
- Inquiries
- Functions
- Portfolio
- Studio
- Account

Logout:
- Click “Logout” in the sidebar to end the session.

### 3.4 Dashboard ("/admin/dashboard")
Purpose:
- Quick studio overview and counts

What you see:
- Upcoming Functions
- New Inquiries
- Pending Albums
- Pending Video Edits
- Pending Deliveries
- Total Uploads

Quick lists:
- Upcoming Functions list
- Recent Inquiries list

Tips:
- Use “View all” to open full Functions or Inquiries lists.

### 3.5 Inquiries ("/admin/inquiries")
Purpose:
- Track customer calls/leads, update their status, and convert to bookings

#### Add inquiry (manual entry)
Steps:
1. Fill Customer name
2. Fill Phone number
3. Fill Occasion
4. Optional: Wanted date
5. Optional: Address
6. Optional: Notes
7. Click “Add inquiry”

#### Filter inquiries by status
Status buttons:
- Pending
- Spoken
- Converted
- Cancelled
- All

Steps:
1. Click a status button.
2. The table updates to show only that status.

#### Update inquiry status
Available actions (depend on current status):
- Mark spoken
- Cancel
- Reopen
- Convert to order
- Delete

Recommended workflow:
1. New lead comes in → keep as Pending
2. After speaking → mark Spoken
3. If confirmed booking → Convert to order
4. If not proceeding → mark Cancelled

Important:
- Delete removes the inquiry permanently.

### 3.6 Functions (Bookings) ("/admin/functions")
Purpose:
- Track every confirmed booking (functions / celebrations) and delivery progress

#### Add Booking
Steps:
1. Click “Add Booking”
2. Fill:
   - Client name
   - Phone number
   - Occasion
   - Event dates (first date is required; add multiple days if needed)
   - Total amount (optional but recommended)
   - Advance received (optional but recommended)
3. Add booking notes (optional)
4. Select Services booked (checkboxes)
5. Select Complimentary gifts (checkboxes)
6. Click “Save This Celebration”

#### View and update an existing booking
For each booking you can update:
- Overall status
- Album status
- Video status

Steps:
1. Open Functions page.
2. Find the booking.
3. Use dropdowns (Overall/Album/Video) to update progress.
4. Use “Details” to view services/complimentary/notes.

Delete booking:
- Click “Delete”
- Confirm the popup
- Booking is removed permanently

### 3.7 Portfolio ("/admin/portfolio")
Purpose:
- Upload and remove photos/videos shown on the public portfolio

#### Upload media
Steps:
1. Select a Category from the dropdown.
2. Click “Upload Media”.
3. Select one or multiple files (images and/or videos).
4. Wait until upload finishes (button shows “Uploading...”).

How media type is chosen:
- If the file is a video (file type starts with “video”), it is saved as video.
- Otherwise it is saved as photo.

#### Delete media
Steps:
1. Find the photo/video thumbnail.
2. Click “Delete”.
3. Confirm the popup.

Important:
- Delete is permanent.
- If a photo/video is used as a category cover image, deleting it may affect the category look.

### 3.8 Studio (Branding & Contact) ("/admin/settings")
Purpose:
- Update what families see on the public website (logo, portrait, testimonials, contact details, counters)

#### Upload studio logo
Requirements:
- PNG format

Steps:
1. In “Studio logo” section, click “Upload logo”
2. Choose a PNG file
3. Wait until upload completes

Remove logo:
1. Click “Remove logo”
2. Confirm

#### Upload owner portrait (About page)
Steps:
1. In “Owner portrait” section, click “Upload portrait”
2. Choose an image file
3. Wait until upload completes

Remove portrait:
1. Click “Remove photo”
2. Confirm

#### Manage testimonials (Kind words)
Add a review:
1. Click “+ Add review”
2. Enter Name (example: “Priya & Arun”)
3. Enter Their words

Remove a review:
1. Click “Remove”

Save changes:
- Click “Save all changes”

#### Update counters (Hearts we’ve touched)
Fields:
- Events covered
- Years of craft
- Happy families

Steps:
1. Edit the values
2. Click “Save all changes”

#### Update contact details
Fields include:
- Email
- Primary mobile
- Secondary mobile
- WhatsApp number
- Instagram URL
- YouTube URL
- Studio address
- Pincode

Steps:
1. Edit details
2. Click “Save all changes”

Notes:
- Contact page uses these details.
- Map is shown only if Google Maps embed is configured in backend settings.

### 3.9 Account ("/admin/account")
Purpose:
- Change admin username and/or password

Steps:
1. Enter Current password (required)
2. Enter New username (optional)
3. Enter New password (optional)
4. Confirm new password (if using new password)
5. Click “Save changes”

Rules:
- You must enter at least a new username or a new password
- New password and confirmation must match

## 4) Common Issues (Quick Fixes)

### 4.1 Website not loading
Check:
- Is the frontend running on port 3000?
- Is the API running on port 8080?

If API is down:
- Home/Portfolio pages may show missing content.

### 4.2 Admin pages keep redirecting to login
Reason:
- Session token is missing or expired.

Fix:
1. Open /admin/login
2. Login again

### 4.3 Uploads not showing
Check:
- API must be running
- Upload storage must be available on the server

## 5) Safety and good practice
- Do not share admin username/password publicly.
- After finishing admin work, always click Logout.
- Keep a backup of uploads and booking data regularly.
